return {
  ["subclass.path-of-the-wild-heart.xphb2024.barbarian.wild-heart.0"]={title="Path of the Wild Heart",subtitle="Subclasse - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 55\n\n=== CARACTERISTICAS DA SUBCLASSE ===\n\nNivel 3 - Animal Speaker\n\nPagina: 55\n\nYou can cast the XPHB and XPHB spells but only as Rituals. Wisdom is your spellcasting ability for them.\n\nNivel 3 - Path of the Wild Heart\n\nPagina: 55\n\nWalk in Community with the Animal World\n\nBarbarians who follow the Path of the Wild Heart view themselves as kin to animals. These Barbarians learn magical means to communicate with animals, and their Rage heightens their connection to animals as it fills them with supernatural might.\n\nNivel 3 - Rage of the Wilds\n\nPagina: 55\n\nYour Rage taps into the primal power of animals. Whenever you activate your Rage, you gain one of the following options of your choice.\n\nBear\n\nWhile your Rage is active, you have XPHB to every damage type except Force, Necrotic, Psychic, and Radiant.\n\nEagle\n\nWhen you activate your Rage, you can take the XPHB and XPHB actions as part of that XPHB. While your Rage is active, you can take a XPHB to take both of those actions.\n\nWolf\n\nWhile your Rage is active, your allies have XPHB on attack rolls against any enemy of yours within 5 feet of you.\n\nNivel 3 - Rage of the Wilds\n\nNivel 6 - Aspect of the Wilds\n\nPagina: 55\n\nYou gain one of the following options of your choice. Whenever you finish a XPHB, you can change your choice.\n\nOwl\n\nYou have XPHB with a range of 60 feet. If you already have XPHB, its range increases by 60 feet.\n\nPanther\n\nYou have a XPHB equal to your XPHB.\n\nSalmon\n\nYou have a XPHB equal to your XPHB.\n\nNivel 6 - Aspect of the Wilds\n\nNivel 10 - Nature Speaker\n\nPagina: 55\n\nYou can cast the XPHB spell but only as a XPHB. Wisdom is your spellcasting ability for it.\n\nNivel 14 - Power of the Wilds\n\nPagina: 55\n\nWhenever you activate your Rage, you gain one of the following options of your choice.\n\nFalcon\n\nWhile your Rage is active, you have a XPHB equal to your XPHB if you aren't wearing any armor.\n\nLion\n\nWhile your Rage is active, any of your enemies within 5 feet of you have XPHB on attack rolls against targets other than you or another Barbarian who has this option active.\n\nRam\n\nWhile your Rage is active, you can cause a Large or smaller creature to have the XPHB condition when you hit it with a melee attack.\n\nNivel 14 - Power of the Wilds"},
  ["feature.path-of-the-wild-heart.xphb2024.barbarian.wild-heart.3"]={title="Path of the Wild Heart",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 55\n\nWalk in Community with the Animal World\n\nBarbarians who follow the Path of the Wild Heart view themselves as kin to animals. These Barbarians learn magical means to communicate with animals, and their Rage heightens their connection to animals as it fills them with supernatural might."},
  ["subclass.path-of-the-world-tree.xphb2024.barbarian.world-tree.0"]={title="Path of the World Tree",subtitle="Subclasse - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 56\n\n=== CARACTERISTICAS DA SUBCLASSE ===\n\nNivel 3 - Path of the World Tree\n\nPagina: 56\n\nTrace the Roots and Branches of the Multiverse\n\nBarbarians who follow the Path of the World Tree connect with the cosmic tree Yggdrasil through their Rage. This tree grows among the Outer Planes, connecting them to each other and the Material Plane. These Barbarians draw on the tree's magic for vitality and as a means of dimensional travel.\n\nNivel 3 - Vitality of the Tree\n\nPagina: 56\n\nYour Rage taps into the life force of the World Tree. You gain the following benefits.\n\nVitality Surge\n\nWhen you activate your Rage, you gain a number of XPHB equal to your Barbarian level.\n\nLife-Giving Force\n\nAt the start of each of your turns while your Rage is active, you can choose another creature within 10 feet of yourself to gain XPHB. To determine the number of XPHB, roll a number of d6s equal to your Rage Damage bonus, and add them together. If any of these XPHB remain when your Rage ends, they vanish.\n\nNivel 3 - Vitality of the Tree\n\nNivel 6 - Branches of the Tree\n\nPagina: 56\n\nWhenever a creature you can see starts its turn within 30 feet of you while your Rage is active, you can take a XPHB to summon spectral branches of the World Tree around it. The target must succeed on a Strength saving throw (8 plus your Strength modifier and XPHB) or be teleported to an unoccupied space you can see within 5 feet of yourself or in the nearest unoccupied space you can see. After the target teleports, you can reduce its XPHB to 0 until the end of the current turn.\n\nNivel 6 - Branches of the Tree\n\nNivel 10 - Battering Roots\n\nPagina: 56\n\nDuring your turn, your reach is 10 feet greater with any items, as tendrils of the World Tree extend from you. When you hit with such a weapon on your turn, you can activate the XPHB or XPHB mastery property in addition to a different mastery property you're using with that weapon.\n\nNivel 10 - Battering Roots\n\nNivel 14 - Travel Along the Tree\n\nPagina: 56\n\nWhen you activate your Rage and as a XPHB while your Rage is active, you can teleport up to 60 feet to an unoccupied space you can see.\n\nIn addition, once per Rage, you can increase the range of that teleport to 150 feet. When you do so, you can also bring up to six willing creatures who are within 10 feet of you. Each creature teleports to an unoccupied space of your choice within 10 feet of your destination space.\n\nNivel 14 - Travel Along the Tree"},
  ["feature.path-of-the-world-tree.xphb2024.barbarian.world-tree.3"]={title="Path of the World Tree",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 56\n\nTrace the Roots and Branches of the Multiverse\n\nBarbarians who follow the Path of the World Tree connect with the cosmic tree Yggdrasil through their Rage. This tree grows among the Outer Planes, connecting them to each other and the Material Plane. These Barbarians draw on the tree's magic for vitality and as a means of dimensional travel."},
  ["subclass.path-of-the-zealot.xge2024.barbarian.zealot.0"]={title="Path of the Zealot",subtitle="Subclasse - XGE - 2024",body="=== CARACTERISTICAS DA SUBCLASSE ===\n\nNivel 3 - Divine Fury\n\nPagina: 11\n\nStarting when you choose this path at 3rd level, you can channel divine fury into your weapon strikes. While you're raging, the first creature you hit on each of your turns with a weapon attack takes extra damage equal to 1d6 + half your barbarian level. The extra damage is necrotic or radiant; you choose the type of damage when you gain this feature.\n\nNivel 3 - Divine Fury\n\nPagina: 57\n\nYou can channel divine power into your strikes. On each of your turns while your Rage is active, the first creature you hit with a weapon or an XPHB takes extra damage equal to 1d6 plus half your Barbarian level (round down). The extra damage is Necrotic or Radiant; you choose the type each time you deal the damage.\n\nNivel 3 - Divine Fury\n\nNivel 3 - Divine Fury\n\nNivel 3 - Path of the Zealot\n\nPagina: 11\n\nSome deities inspire their followers to pitch themselves into a ferocious battle fury. These barbarians are zealots—warriors who channel their rage into powerful displays of divine power.\n\nA variety of gods across the worlds of D&D inspire their followers to embrace this path. Tempus from the Forgotten Realms and Hextor and Erythnul of Greyhawk are all prime examples. In general, the gods who inspire zealots are deities of combat, destruction, and violence. Not all are evil, but few are good.\n\nNivel 3 - Path of the Zealot\n\nPagina: 57\n\nRage in Ecstatic Union with a God\n\nBarbarians who walk the Path of the Zealot receive boons from a god or pantheon. These Barbarians experience their Rage as an ecstatic episode of divine union that infuses them with power. They are often allies to the priests and other followers of their god or pantheon.\n\nNivel 3 - Warrior of the Gods\n\nPagina: 11\n\nAt 3rd level, your soul is marked for endless battle. If a spell, such as raise dead, has the sole effect of restoring you to life (but not undeath), the caster doesn't need material components to cast the spell on you.\n\nNivel 3 - Warrior of the Gods\n\nPagina: 57\n\nA divine entity helps ensure you can continue the fight. You have a pool of four d12s that you can spend to heal yourself. As a XPHB, you can expend dice from the pool, roll them, and regain a number of XPHB equal to the roll's total.\n\nYour pool regains all expended dice when you finish a XPHB.\n\nThe pool's maximum number of dice increases by one when you reach Barbarian levels 6 (5 dice), 12 (6 dice), and 17 (7 dice).\n\nNivel 3 - Warrior of the Gods\n\nNivel 6 - Fanatical Focus\n\nPagina: 11\n\nStarting at 6th level, the divine power that fuels your rage can protect you. If you fail a saving throw while you're raging, you can reroll it, and you must use the new roll. You can use this ability only once per rage.\n\nNivel 6 - Fanatical Focus\n\nPagina: 57\n\nOnce per active Rage, if you fail a saving throw, you can reroll it with a bonus equal to your Rage Damage bonus, and you must use the new roll.\n\nNivel 10 - Zealous Presence\n\nPagina: 11\n\nAt 10th level, you learn to channel divine power to inspire zealotry in others. As a bonus action, you unleash a battle cry infused with divine energy. Up to ten other creatures of your choice within 60 feet of you that can hear you gain advantage on attack rolls and saving throws until the start of your next turn.\n\nOnce you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a long rest.\n\nNivel 10 - Zealous Presence\n\nPagina: 57\n\nAs a XPHB, you unleash a battle cry infused with divine energy. Up to ten other creatures of your choice within 60 feet of you gain XPHB on attack rolls and saving throws until the start of your next turn.\n\nOnce you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a XPHB unless you expend a use of your Rage (no action required) to restore your use of it.\n\nNivel 10 - Zealous Presence\n\nNivel 14 - Rage beyond Death\n\nPagina: 11\n\nBeginning at 14th level, the divine power that fuels your rage allows you to shrug off fatal blows.\n\nWhile you're raging, having 0 hit points doesn't knock you unconscious. You still must make death saving throws, and you suffer the normal effects of taking damage while at 0 hit points. However, if you would die due to failing death saving throws, you don't die until your rage ends, and you die then only if you still have 0 hit points.\n\nNivel 14 - Rage of the Gods\n\nPagina: 57\n\nWhen you activate your Rage, you can assume the form of a divine warrior. This form lasts for 1 minute or until you drop to 0 XPHB. Once you use this feature, you can't do so again until you finish a XPHB.\n\nWhile in this form, you gain the benefits below.\n\nFlight\n\nYou have a XPHB equal to your XPHB and can hover.\n\nResistance\n\nYou have XPHB to Necrotic, Psychic, and Radiant damage.\n\nRevivification\n\nWhen a creature within 30 feet of you would drop to 0 XPHB, you can take a XPHB to expend a use of your Rage to instead change the target's XPHB to a number equal to your Barbarian level.\n\nNivel 14 - Rage of the Gods"},
  ["feature.path-of-the-zealot.xge2024.barbarian.zealot.3"]={title="Path of the Zealot",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 11\n\nSome deities inspire their followers to pitch themselves into a ferocious battle fury. These barbarians are zealots—warriors who channel their rage into powerful displays of divine power.\n\nA variety of gods across the worlds of D&D inspire their followers to embrace this path. Tempus from the Forgotten Realms and Hextor and Erythnul of Greyhawk are all prime examples. In general, the gods who inspire zealots are deities of combat, destruction, and violence. Not all are evil, but few are good."},
