f a spell, such as raise dead, has the sole effect of restoring you to life (but not undeath), the caster doesn't need material components to cast the spell on you.\n\nNivel 3 - Warrior of the Gods\n\nPagina: 57\n\nA divine entity helps ensure you can continue the fight. You have a pool of four d12s that you can spend to heal yourself. As a XPHB, you can expend dice from the pool, roll them, and regain a number of XPHB equal to the roll's total.\n\nYour pool regains all expended dice when you finish a XPHB.\n\nThe pool's maximum number of dice increases by one when you reach Barbarian levels 6 (5 dice), 12 (6 dice), and 17 (7 dice).\n\nNivel 3 - Warrior of the Gods\n\nNivel 6 - Fanatical Focus\n\nPagina: 11\n\nStarting at 6th level, the divine power that fuels your rage can protect you. If you fail a saving throw while you're raging, you can reroll it, and you must use the new roll. You can use this ability only once per rage.\n\nNivel 6 - Fanatical Focus\n\nPagina: 57\n\nOnce per active Rage, if you fail a saving throw, you can reroll it with a bonus equal to your Rage Damage bonus, and you must use the new roll.\n\nNivel 10 - Zealous Presence\n\nPagina: 11\n\nAt 10th level, you learn to channel divine power to inspire zealotry in others. As a bonus action, you unleash a battle cry infused with divine energy. Up to ten other creatures of your choice within 60 feet of you that can hear you gain advantage on attack rolls and saving throws until the start of your next turn.\n\nOnce you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a long rest.\n\nNivel 10 - Zealous Presence\n\nPagina: 57\n\nAs a XPHB, you unleash a battle cry infused with divine energy. Up to ten other creatures of your choice within 60 feet of you gain XPHB on attack rolls and saving throws until the start of your next turn.\n\nOnce you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a XPHB unless you expend a use of your Rage (no action required) to restore your use of it.\n\nNivel 10 - Zealous Presence\n\nNivel 14 - Rage beyond Death\n\nPagina: 11\n\nBeginning at 14th level, the divine power that fuels your rage allows you to shrug off fatal blows.\n\nWhile you're raging, having 0 hit points doesn't knock you unconscious. You still must make death saving throws, and you suffer the normal effects of taking damage while at 0 hit points. However, if you would die due to failing death saving throws, you don't die until your rage ends, and you die then only if you still have 0 hit points.\n\nNivel 14 - Rage of the Gods\n\nPagina: 57\n\nWhen you activate your Rage, you can assume the form of a divine warrior. This form lasts for 1 minute or until you drop to 0 XPHB. Once you use this feature, you can't do so again until you finish a XPHB.\n\nWhile in this form, you gain the benefits below.\n\nFlight\n\nYou have a XPHB equal to your XPHB and can hover.\n\nResistance\n\nYou have XPHB to Necrotic, Psychic, and Radiant damage.\n\nRevivification\n\nWhen a creature within 30 feet of you would drop to 0 XPHB, you can take a XPHB to expend a use of your Rage to instead change the target's XPHB to a number equal to your Barbarian level.\n\nNivel 14 - Rage of the Gods"},
  ["feature.path-of-the-zealot.xphb2024.barbarian.zealot.3"]={title="Path of the Zealot",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 57\n\nRage in Ecstatic Union with a God\n\nBarbarians who walk the Path of the Zealot receive boons from a god or pantheon. These Barbarians experience their Rage as an ecstatic episode of divine union that infuses them with power. They are often allies to the priests and other followers of their god or pantheon."},
  ["subclass.path-of-wild-magic.tce2014.barbarian.wild-magic.0"]={title="Path of Wild Magic",subtitle="Subclasse - TCE - 2014",body="=== CARACTERISTICAS DA SUBCLASSE ===\n\nNivel 3 - Magic Awareness\n\nPagina: 25\n\n3rd-level Path of Wild Magic feature\n\nAs an action, you can open your awareness to the presence of concentrated magic. Until the end of your next turn, you know the location of any spell or magic item within 60 feet of you that isn't behind Cover. When you sense a spell, you learn which school of magic it belongs to.\n\nYou can use this feature a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest.\n\nNivel 3 - Magic Awareness\n\nNivel 3 - Path of Wild Magic\n\nPagina: 25\n\nMany places in the multiverse abound with beauty, intense emotion, and rampant magic; the Feywild, the Upper Planes, and other realms of supernatural power radiate with such forces and can profoundly influence people. As folk of deep feeling, barbarians are especially susceptible to these wild influences, with some barbarians being transformed by the magic. These magic-suffused barbarians walk the Path of Wild Magic. Elf, tiefling, aasimar, and genasi barbarians often seek this path, eager to manifest the otherworldly magic of their ancestors.\n\nNivel 3 - Wild Surge\n\nPagina: 25\n\n3rd-level Path of Wild Magic feature\n\nThe magical energy roiling inside you sometimes erupts from you. When you enter your rage, roll on the Wild Magic table to determine the magical effect produced.\n\nIf the effect requires a saving throw, the DC equals 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Constitution modifier.\n\nd8 | Magical Effect\n\n1 | Shadowy tendrils lash around you. Each creature of your choice that you can see within 30 feet of you must succeed on a Constitution saving throw or take 1d12 necrotic damage. You also gain 1d12 temporary hit points.\n\n2 | You teleport up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space you can see. Until your rage ends, you can use this effect again on each of your turns as a bonus action.\n\n3 | An intangible spirit, which looks like a flumph or a pixie (your choice), appears within 5 feet of one creature of your choice that you can see within 30 feet of you. At the end of the current turn, the spirit explodes, and each creature within 5 feet of it must succeed on a Dexterity saving throw or take 1d6 force damage. Until your rage ends, you can use this effect again, summoning another spirit, on each of your turns as a bonus action.\n\n4 | Magic infuses one weapon of your choice that you are holding. Until your rage ends, the weapon's damage type changes to force, and it gains the light and thrown properties, with a normal range of 20 feet and a long range of 60 feet. If the weapon leaves your hand, the weapon reappears in your hand at the end of the current turn.\n\n5 | Whenever a creature hits you with an attack roll before your rage ends, that creature takes 1d6 force damage, as magic lashes out in retribution.\n\n6 | Until your rage ends, you are surrounded by multi colored, protective lights; you gain a +1 bonus to AC, and while within 10 feet of you, your allies gain the same bonus.\n\n7 | Flowers and vines temporarily grow around you. Until your rage ends, the ground within 15 feet of you is difficult terrain for your enemies.\n\n8 | A bolt of light shoots from your chest. Another creature of your choice that you can see within 30 feet of you must succeed on a Constitution saving throw or take 1d6 radiant damage and be blinded until the start of your next turn. Until your rage ends, you can use this effect again on each of your turns as a bonus action.\n\nNivel 6 - Bolstering Magic\n\nPagina: 25\n\n6th-level Path of Wild Magic feature\n\nYou can harness your wild magic to bolster yourself or a companion. As an action, you can touch one creature (which can be yourself) and confer one of the following benefits of your choice to that creature:\n\n• For 10 minutes, the creature can roll a d3 whenever making an attack roll or an ability check and add the number rolled to the d20 roll.\n\n• Roll a d3. The creature regains one expended spell slot, the level of which equals the number rolled or lower (the creature's choice). Once a creature receives this benefit, that creature can't receive it again until after a long rest.\n\nYou can take this action a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest.\n\nNivel 10 - Unstable Backlash\n\nPagina: 25\n\n10th-level Path of Wild Magic feature\n\nWhen you are imperiled during your rage, the magic within you can lash out; immediately after you take damage or fail a saving throw while raging, you can use your reaction to roll on the Wild Magic table and immediately produce the effect rolled. This effect replaces your current Wild Magic effect.\n\nNivel 14 - Controlled Surge\n\nPagina: 25\n\n14th-level Path of Wild Magic feature\n\nWhenever you roll on the Wild Magic table, you can roll the die twice and choose which of the two effects to unleash. If you roll the same number on both dice, you can ignore the number and choose any effect on the table."},
  ["feature.path-of-wild-magic.tce2014.barbarian.wild-magic.3"]={title="Path of Wild Magic",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 25\n\nMany places in the multiverse abound with beauty, intense emotion, and rampant magic; the Feywild, the Upper Planes, and other realms of supernatural power radiate with such forces and can profoundly influence people. As folk of deep feeling, barbarians are especially susceptible to these wild influences, with some barbarians being transformed by the magic. These magic-suffused barbarians walk the Path of Wild Magic. Elf, tiefling, aasimar, and genasi barbarians often seek this path, eager to manifest the otherworldly magic of their ancestors."},
  ["feature.path-to-the-grave.rhw2014.cleric.grave.3"]={title="Path to the Grave",subtitle="Caracteristica - RHW - 2014",body=""},
  ["magicitem.pathfinder-s-greataxe.pota2014"]={title="Pathfinder's Greataxe",subtitle="Item Magico - PotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 175\n\nRaridade: unknown (magic)\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nWhen you wield this +1 greataxe, you always know the way to the nearest passage leading from underground toward the surface, as well as the approximate depth the axe is underground."},
  ["feature.patient-defense.phb2014.monk.base.2"]={title="Patient Defense",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 76\n\nYou can spend 1 ki point to take the Dodge action as a bonus action on your turn."},
  ["feature.patient-defense.xphb2024.monk.base.2"]={title="Patient Defense",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["creature.patrina-velikovna.cos2014"]={title="Patrina Velikovna",subtitle="Criatura - CoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 89\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid"},
  ["creature.pazrodine.bmt2014"]={title="Pazrodine",subtitle="Criatura - BMT - 2014",body="Pagina: 113\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / G\n\nCR: 21\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 330 (20d20 + 120)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 80\n\nSTR 22 | DEX 18 | CON 23 | INT 20 | WIS 22 | CHA 26\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: all, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nGuardian of the Market\n\nPazrodine can sense when an item is stolen from Seelie Market. She knows the distance and direction to stolen items, as if by the Locate Object spell.\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf Pazrodine fails a saving throw, she can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nPazrodine makes one Bite attack and two Claw attacks.\n\nBite\n\nmw 13 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h17 (2d10 + 6) piercing damage plus 11 (2d10) radiant damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 13 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h13 (2d6 + 6) slashing damage.\n\nTail\n\nmw 13 to hit, reach 20 ft., one target. h10 (1d8 + 6) bludgeoning damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 21 Strength saving throw or have the prone condition.\n\nBreath Weapon {@recharge 5}\n\nPazrodine uses one of the following breath weapons:\n\n• Dream Breath Pazrodine exhales mist in a 90-foot cone. Each creature in that area must succeed on a 21 Constitution saving throw or have the unconscious condition for 10 minutes. This effect ends for a creature if the creature takes damage or someone uses an action to wake it.\n\n• Moonlight Breath Pazrodine exhales a beam of moonlight in a 120-foot line that is 10 feet wide. Each creature in that area must make a 21 Dexterity saving throw, taking 60 (11d10) radiant damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nTail\n\nPazrodine makes one Tail attack.\n\nCast a Spell (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nPazrodine uses Spellcasting."},
  ["creature.pazuzu.mabjov2014"]={title="Pazuzu",subtitle="Criatura - MaBJoV - 2014",body="Pagina: 104\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / L\n\nCR: 25\n\nCA: 21\n\nPV: 405 (30d10 + 240)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 90\n\nSTR 23 | DEX 30 | CON 27 | INT 23 | WIS 18 | CHA 27\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: all, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: acid, cold, fire\n\nImunidades: lightning, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAura of Servile Avians\n\nAny evil creature with a natural fly speed and a CR of 20 or less must make a 21 Wisdom saving throw if they attempt to attack Pazuzu. A failed save means their action is wasted and the attack fails. On a successful saving throw the target is immune to this effect in the future.\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf Pazuzu fails a saving throw, he can choose to succeed instead.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nPazuzu has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nMagic Weapons\n\nPazuzu's weapon attacks are magical.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nPazuzu makes two Greatsword or Talon attacks.\n\nGreatsword\n\nmw 14 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h13 (2d6 + 6) slashing damage plus 7 (2d6) necrotic damage.\n\nTalon\n\nmw 14 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h15 (2d8 + 6) slashing damage plus 9 (2d8) poison damage.\n\nBreath Weapons {@recharge 5}\n\nPazuzu exhales poisonous acid in a 100-foot line that is 5 feet wide. Every creature hit by the acid must make a 21 Dexterity saving throw, taking 70 (20d6) acid damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. A creature killed by this breath weapon melts and is disintegrated.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nDispel\n\nPazuzu casts dispel magic, automatically dispelling any spell of 6th level or lower on the target.\n\nHasted Greatsword\n\nPazuzu uses his magic greatsword to grant him the following abilities until the start of his next turn. Pazuzu's speed is now doubled, he gains a +2 bonus to AC, has advantage on Dexterity saving throws, and gains one additional Greatsword attack.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nDisarm\n\nPazuzu attempts to knock a weapon out of a target's hand. He makes a Greatsword attack and if it hits, the target does not take damage but instead must make a 22 Strength saving throw. If the target fails the saving throw, the targeted weapon flies 10 feet away in a random direction.\n\nLethal Leap\n\nPazuzu attacks once with his Greatsword or Talon and then may fly up to 60 feet away. Pazuzu's movement does not provoke opportunity attacks."},
  ["subclass.peace-domain.tce2014.cleric.peace.0"]={title="Peace Domain",subtitle="Subclasse - TCE - 2014",body="=== CARACTERISTICAS DA SUBCLASSE ===\n\nNivel 1 - Emboldening Bond\n\nPagina: 32\n\n1st-level Peace Domain feature\n\nYou can forge an empowering bond among people who are at peace with one another. As an action, you choose a number of willing creatures within 30 feet of you (this can include yourself) equal to your proficiency bonus. You create a magical bond among them for 10 minutes or until you use this feature again. While any bonded creature is within 30 feet of another, the creature can roll a d4 and add the number rolled to an attack roll, an ability check, or a saving throw it makes. Each creature can add the d4 no more than once per turn.\n\nYou can use this feature a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest.\n\nNivel 1 - Emboldening Bond\n\nNivel 1 - Implement of Peace\n\nPagina: 32\n\n1st-level Peace Domain feature\n\nYou gain proficiency in the Insight, Performance, or Persuasion skill (your choice).\n\nNivel 1 - Implement of Peace\n\nNivel 1 - Peace Domain\n\nPagina: 32\n\nThe balm of peace thrives at the heart of healthy communities, between friendly nations, and in the souls of the kindhearted. The gods of peace inspire people of all sorts to resolve conflict and to stand up against those forces that try to prevent peace from flourishing. See the Peace Deities table for a list of some of the gods associated with this domain.\n\nClerics of the Peace Domain preside over the signing of treaties, and they are often asked to arbitrate in disputes. These clerics' blessings draw people together and help them shoulder one another's burdens, and the clerics' magic aids those who are driven to fight for the way of peace.\n\nExample Deity | Pantheon\n\nElven | Elven\n\nDwarven | Dwarven\n\nEberron | Eberron\n\nHalfling | Halfling\n\nEldath | Forgotten Realms\n\nGnomish | Gnomish\n\nDragonlance | Dragonlance\n\nGreyhawk | Greyhawk\n\nDomain Spells\n\n1st-level Peace Domain feature\n\nYou gain domain spells at the cleric levels listed in the Peace Domain Spells table. See the Divine Domain class feature for how domain spells work.\n\nCleric Level | Spells\n\n1st | heroism, sanctuary\n\n3rd | aid, warding bond\n\n5th | beacon of hope, sending\n\n7th | aura of purity, Otiluke's resilient sphere\n\n9th | greater restoration, Rary's telepathic bond\n\nNivel 2 - Channel Divinity: Balm of Peace\n\nPagina: 32\n\n2nd-level Peace Domain feature\n\nYou can use your Channel Divinity to make your very presence a soothing balm. As an action, you can move up to your speed, without provoking opportunity attacks, and when you move within 5 feet of any other creature during this action, you can restore a number of hit points to that creature equal to 2d6 + your Wisdom modifier (minimum of 1 hit point). A creature can receive this healing only once whenever you take this action.\n\nNivel 3 - Channel Divinity: Balm of Peace\n\nNivel 3 - Peace Domain\n\nNivel 6 - Protective Bond\n\nPagina: 32\n\n6th-level Peace Domain feature\n\nThe bond you forge between people helps them protect each other. When a creature affected by your Emboldening Bond feature is about to take damage, a second bonded creature within 30 feet of the first can use its reaction to teleport to an unoccupied space within 5 feet of the first creature. The second creature then takes all the damage instead.\n\nNivel 8 - Blessed Strikes\n\nPagina: 32\n\n{@i 8th-level cleric tce, which replaces the Potent Spellcasting feature\n\nYou are blessed with divine might in battle. When a creature takes damage from one of your cantrips or weapon attacks, you can also deal 1d8 radiant damage to that creature. Once you deal this damage, you can't use this feature again until the start of your next turn.\n\nNivel 8 - Potent Spellcasting\n\nPagina: 32\n\n8th-level Peace Domain feature\n\nYou add your Wisdom modifier to the damage you deal with any cleric cantrip.\n\nNivel 17 - Expansive Bond\n\nPagina: 32\n\n17th-level Peace Domain feature\n\nThe benefits of your Emboldening Bond and Protective Bond features now work when the creatures are within 60 feet of each other. Moreover, when a creature uses Protective Bond to take someone else's damage, the creature has resistance to that damage."},
  ["feature.peace-domain.tce2014.cleric.peace.1"]={title="Peace Domain",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 32\n\nThe balm of peace thrives at the heart of healthy communities, between friendly nations, and in the souls of the kindhearted. The gods of peace inspire people of all sorts to resolve conflict and to stand up against those forces that try to prevent peace from flourishing. See the Peace Deities table for a list of some of the gods associated with this domain.\n\nClerics of the Peace Domain preside over the signing of treaties, and they are often asked to arbitrate in disputes. These clerics' blessings draw people together and help them shoulder one another's burdens, and the clerics' magic aids those who are driven to fight for the way of peace.\n\nExample Deity | Pantheon\n\nElven | Elven\n\nDwarven | Dwarven\n\nEberron | Eberron\n\nHalfling | Halfling\n\nEldath | Forgotten Realms\n\nGnomish | Gnomish\n\nDragonlance | Dragonlance\n\nGreyhawk | Greyhawk\n\nDomain Spells\n\n1st-level Peace Domain feature\n\nYou gain domain spells at the cleric levels listed in the Peace Domain Spells table. See the Divine Domain class feature for how domain spells work.\n\nCleric Level | Spells\n\n1st | heroism, sanctuary\n\n3rd | aid, warding bond\n\n5th | beacon of hope, sending\n\n7th | aura of purity, Otiluke's resilient sphere\n\n9th | greater restoration, Rary's telepathic bond"},
  ["feature.peace-domain.tce2014.cleric.peace.3"]={title="Peace Domain",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body=""},
  ["creature.peacock.bgdia2014"]={title="Peacock",subtitle="Criatura - BGDIA - 2014",body="Pagina: 195\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["item.pearl.dmg2014"]={title="Pearl",subtitle="Item - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 134\n\nRaridade: none\n\nAn opaque lustrous white, yellow, or pink gemstone."},
  ["item.pearl.xdmg2024"]={title="Pearl",subtitle="Item - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 214\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA lustrous white, yellow, or pink gemstone."},
  ["magicitem.pearl-of-power.dmg2014"]={title="Pearl of Power",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 184\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nWhile this pearl is on your person, you can use an action to speak its command word and regain one expended spell slot. If the expended slot was of 4th level or higher, the new slot is 3rd level. Once you have used the pearl, it can't be used again until the next dawn."},
  ["magicitem.pearl-of-power.xdmg2024"]={title="Pearl of Power",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 284\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nWhile this pearl is on your person, you can take a XPHB action to regain one expended spell slot of level 3 or lower. Once you use the pearl, it can't be used again until the next dawn."},
  ["magicitem.pearl-of-undead-detection.wdmm2014"]={title="Pearl of Undead Detection",subtitle="Item Magico - WDMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 76\n\nRaridade: unknown (magic)\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nThis black pearl glows faintly when undead are within 120 feet of it."},
  ["creature.pech.ditlcot2014"]={title="Pech",subtitle="Criatura - DitLCoT - 2014",body="Pagina: 16\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: elemental / S\n\nCR: 4\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 82 (11d6 + 44)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, burrow: 20\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 11 | CON 18 | INT 11 | WIS 14 | CHA 10\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft., tremorsense 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Terran\n\nImunidades a condicoes: petrified\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe pech has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nSunlight Sensitivity\n\nWhile in sunlight, the pech has disadvantage on attack rolls.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nCommunal Spellcasting (2/Day)\n\nStone Shape (3/Day)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe pech makes two Fortified Pickaxe attacks. If it hits a Large or smaller creature with both attacks, the target must succeed on a 14 Strength saving throw or have the prone condition.\n\nFortified Pickaxe\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h11 (2d6 + 4) force damage. If the target is a Construct or an object, the attack is automatically a critical hit."},
  ["creature.pech.qftis2014"]={title="Pech",subtitle="Criatura - QftIS - 2014",body="Pagina: 213\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: elemental / S\n\nCR: 4\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 82 (11d6 + 44)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, burrow: 20\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 11 | CON 18 | INT 11 | WIS 14 | CHA 10\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft., tremorsense 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Terran\n\nImunidades a condicoes: petrified\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe pech has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nSunlight Sensitivity\n\nWhile in sunlight, the pech has disadvantage on attack rolls.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nCommunal Spellcasting (2/Day)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe pech makes two Fortified Pickaxe attacks. If it hits a Large or smaller creature with both attacks, the target must succeed on a 14 Strength saving throw or have the prone condition.\n\nFortified Pickaxe\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h11 (2d6 + 4) force damage. If the target is a Construct or an object, the attack is automatically a critical hit.\n\nStone Shape (3/Day)\n\nThe pech casts Stone Shape, requiring no spell components and using Wisdom as the spellcasting ability."},
  ["creature.peebles.oota2014"]={title="Peebles",subtitle="Criatura - OotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 134\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["feature.peerless-athlete.tce2014.paladin.glory.3"]={title="Peerless Athlete",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 53\n\nAs a bonus action, you can use your Channel Divinity to augment your athleticism. For the next 10 minutes, you have advantage on Strength (Athletics) and Dexterity (Acrobatics) checks; you can carry, push, drag, and lift twice as much weight as normal; and the distance of your long and high jumps increases by 10 feet (this extra distance costs movement as normal)."},
  ["feature.peerless-athlete.xphb2024.paladin.glory.3"]={title="Peerless Athlete",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["feature.peerless-skill.phb2014.bard.lore.14"]={title="Peerless Skill",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 54\n\nStarting at 14th level, when you make an ability check, you can expend one use of Bardic Inspiration. Roll a Bardic Inspiration die and add the number rolled to your ability check. You can choose to do so after you roll the die for the ability check, but before the DM tells you whether you succeed or fail."},
  ["feature.peerless-skill.xphb2024.bard.lore.14"]={title="Peerless Skill",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["creature.pegasus.mm2014"]={title="Pegasus",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 250\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: celestial / L\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 59 (7d10 + 21)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 60, fly: 90\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 15 | CON 16 | INT 10 | WIS 15 | CHA 13\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: understands Celestial, Common, Elvish, and Sylvan but can't speak\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nHooves\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h11 (2d6 + 4) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["creature.pegasus.xmm2024"]={title="Pegasus",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 235\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: celestial / L\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 59 (7d10 + 21)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 60, fly: 90\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 15 | CON 16 | INT 10 | WIS 15 | CHA 13\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: understands Celestial, Common, Elvish, and Sylvan but can't speak\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nHooves\n\nm 6, reach 5 ft. h7 (1d6 + 4) Bludgeoning damage plus 5 (2d4) Radiant damage."},
  ["deity.pelor.dmg2014"]={title="Pelor",subtitle="Divindade - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 10"},
  ["deity.pelor.egw2014"]={title="Pelor",subtitle="Divindade - EGW - 2014",body="Pagina: 24\n\nPelor rules over sun and summer, his vigil encircling the ages as the keeper of time. As lord of agriculture and harbinger of the harvest, he is worshiped by farmers and most common folk, and his priests are welcomed in many lands. Supporter of the needy and destroyer of evil, the Dawn Father is often the patron of paladins and rangers who follow a similar creed. He is also known for his defeat of the Chained Oblivion and is revered by those who hunt aberrations.\n\nPelor is often found within the Fortress of the Sun, a shining, golden citadel that brings vibrant life to the limitless orchards of the Blessed Fields of Elysium.\n\nDepictions\n\nTapestries of old match early texts describing Pelor as a paternal figure in silver and gold armor, his head a beacon of light and fire so bright that his face can barely be seen. Many statues in holy places use the head as a brazier, lit with each dawn and extinguished at dusk.\n\nHoly Day\n\nPelor's holy day is called Highsummer, and takes place on the fifteenth day of the seventh month. While other parts of Exandria feast, the Dwendalian Empire uses this day as an opportunity to enlist more soldiers in its army. The military holds great feasts and hands out toy soldiers and other propaganda, encouraging people to enlist and help fight against the evil that threatens the king.\n\nCommandments of Pelor\n\n• Be ever vigilant for evil. People are quick to forget the lessons of the past.\n\n• Help relieve the suffering of the innocent.\n\n• Deliver the light of Pelor where darkness dwells, with kindness, compassion, and mercy."},
  ["deity.pelor.phb2014"]={title="Pelor",subtitle="Divindade - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 295"},
  ["deity.pelor.xdmg2024"]={title="Pelor",subtitle="Divindade - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 148"},
  ["creature.pelyious-avhoste.mabjov2014"]={title="Pelyious Avhoste",subtitle="Criatura - MaBJoV - 2014",body="Pagina: 120\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 9\n\nCA: 12/15\n\nPV: 143 (22d8 + 44)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, swim: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 14 | CON 14 | INT 17 | WIS 11 | CHA 13\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nHold Breath\n\nPelyious can hold his breath for 15 minutes.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack (Humanoid or Hybrid Form)\n\nIn Humanoid form, Pelyious makes two Scimitar attacks or two Hand Crossbow attacks. In hybrid form, he can substitute one Scimitar attack for a Bite attack.\n\nScimitar (Humanoid or Hybrid Form)\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d6 + 4) slashing damage plus 7 (2d6) poison damage.\n\nHand Crossbow (Humanoid or Hybrid Form)\n\nrw 6 to hit, range 30/90 ft., one target. h6 (1d6 + 3) piercing damage plus 7 (2d6) poison damage.\n\nBite (Hybrid Form Only)\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h9 (1d10 + 4) piercing damage. If the target is Medium or smaller, it is grappled (escape 16) and until this grapple ends, the target is restrained, and Pelyious can't Bite another target.\n\nChange Shape\n\nPelyious polymorphs into a crocodile-humanoid hybrid, or back into his true form, which is Humanoid. His statistics are the same in each form. Any equipment he is wearing or carrying isn't transformed. He reverts to his true form if he dies.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nSlippery Step (2/Day)\n\nPelyious teleports up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space he can see and may use Change Shape."},
  ["creature.pendragon-beestinger.ai2014"]={title="Pendragon Beestinger",subtitle="Criatura - AI - 2014",body="Pagina: 206\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 12/15\n\nPV: 27 (5d8 + 5)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 14 | CON 12 | INT 17 | WIS 10 | CHA 11\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic, Elvish, Halfling\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nEcho Spell (1/Day)\n\nPendragon can cast the spell he cast on his last turn, whose casting time becomes 1 bonus action. This bonus casting uses a spell slot as normal.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nShortsword\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) piercing damage."},
  ["magicitem.pennant-of-the-vind-rune.skt2014"]={title="Pennant of the Vind Rune",subtitle="Item Magico - SKT - 2014",body="Pagina: 235\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nThis blue pennant is crafted from silk and is five feet long and whips about as if buffeted by a wind. The vind (wind) rune appears on its surface, looking almost like a cloud. The pennant has the following properties, which work only while it's on your person.\n\nWind Step\n\nAs an action, you fly up to 20 feet. If you don't land at the end of this flight, you fall unless you have another means of staying aloft.\n\nComforting Wind\n\nYou can't suffocate.\n\nWinds Grasp\n\nAs a reaction when you fall, you can cause yourself to take no damage from the fall. Once you use this property, you can't use it again until you finish a short or long rest.\n\nWind Walker\n\nWhile you are attuned to this rune, you can cast levitate as a bonus action. Once you use this property, you can't use it again until you finish a short or long rest.\n\nGift of Wind\n\nYou can transfer the pennant's magic to a nonmagical item—a suit of armor, a pair of boots, or a cloak—by tracing the vind rune there with your finger. The transfer takes 8 hours of work that requires the two items to be within 5 feet of each other. At the end, the pennant is destroyed, and the rune appears in silver on the chosen item, which gains a benefit based on its form:\n\n• Armor\n\n• Boots/Cloak"},
  ["creature.pentadrone.mm2014"]={title="Pentadrone",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 226\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / L\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 32 (5d10 + 5)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 14 | CON 12 | INT 10 | WIS 10 | CHA 13\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Modron\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAxiomatic Mind\n\nThe pentadrone can't be compelled to act in a manner contrary to its nature or its instructions.\n\nDisintegration\n\nIf the pentadrone dies, its body disintegrates into dust, leaving behind its weapons and anything else it was carrying.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe pentadrone makes five arm attacks.\n\nArm\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) bludgeoning damage.\n\nParalysis Gas {@recharge 5}\n\nThe pentadrone exhales a 30-foot cone of gas. Each creature in that area must succeed on a 11 Constitution saving throw or be paralyzed for 1 minute. A creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success."},
  ["item.pepper.phb2014"]={title="Pepper",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 157\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["item.pepper.xdmg2024"]={title="Pepper",subtitle="Item - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 213\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["magicitem.peregrine-mask.ggr2014"]={title="Peregrine Mask",subtitle="Item Magico - GGR - 2014",body="Pagina: 180\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nWhile wearing this winged helm, you have a flying speed of 60 feet. In addition, you have advantage on initiative rolls."},
  ["feature.perfect-focus.xphb2024.monk.base.15"]={title="Perfect Focus",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 103\n\nWhen you roll XPHB and don't use Uncanny Metabolism, you regain expended Focus Points until you have 4 if you have 3 or fewer."},
  ["feature.perfect-self.phb2014.monk.base.20"]={title="Perfect Self",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 76\n\nAt 20th level, when you roll for initiative and have no ki points remaining, you regain 4 ki points."},
  ["feature.perfected-armor.efa2014.artificer.armorer.15"]={title="Perfected Armor",subtitle="Caracteristica - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 16\n\nYour Arcane Armor gains additional benefits based on its model, as detailed below.\n\nDreadnaught\n\nThe damage die of your Force Demolisher increases to 2d6 Force damage.\n\nIn addition, when you use your Giant Stature, your reach increases by 10 feet, your size can increase to Large or Huge (your choice), and you have XPHB on Strength checks and Strength saving throws for the duration.\n\nGuardian\n\nThe damage die of your Thunder Pulse increases to 1d10 Thunder damage.\n\nIn addition, when a Huge or smaller creature you can see ends its turn within 30 feet of you, you can take a XPHB to magically force that creature to make a Strength saving throw against your spell save DC. On a failed save, you pull the creature up to 25 feet directly toward you to an unoccupied space. If you pull the target to a space within 5 feet of yourself, you can make a melee weapon attack against it as part of this XPHB.\n\nYou can take this XPHB a number of times equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum of once), and you regain all expended uses when you finish a XPHB.\n\nInfiltrator\n\nThe damage die of your Lightning Launcher increases to 2d6 Lightning damage. Any creature that takes Lightning damage from your Lightning Launcher glimmers with magical light until the start of your next turn. The glimmering creature sheds XPHB in a 5-foot radius, and it has XPHB on attack rolls against you, as the light jolts it if it attacks you.\n\nAdditionally, as a XPHB, you can gain a XPHB equal to twice your XPHB until the end of the current turn. You can take this XPHB a number of times equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum of once), and you regain all expended uses when you finish a XPHB."},
  ["feature.perfected-armor.tce2014.artificer.armorer.15"]={title="Perfected Armor",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 15\n\n15th-level Armorer feature\n\nYour Arcane Armor gains additional benefits based on its model, as shown below."},
  ["feature.perfected-bond.ftd2014.ranger.drakewarden.15"]={title="Perfected Bond",subtitle="Caracteristica - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 15\n\n15th-level Drakewarden feature\n\nYour bond to your drake reaches the pinnacle of its power. While your drake is summoned, you and the drake gain the following benefits:\n\n• Empowered Bite The drake's Bite attack deals an extra 1d6 damage of the type chosen for its Draconic Essence (for a total of 2d6 extra damage).\n\n• Large Drake The drake grows to Large size. When you ride your drake, it is no longer prohibited from using the flying speed of Bond of Fang and Scale.\n\n• Reflexive Resistance When either you or the drake takes damage while you're within 30 feet of each other, you can use your reaction to give yourself or the drake resistance to that instance of damage. You can use this reaction a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."},
  ["feature.performance-of-creation.tce2014.bard.creation.3"]={title="Performance of Creation",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body=""},
  ["creature.performer.xmm2024"]={title="Performer",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 236\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S/M\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 27 (5d8 + 5)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 16 | CON 12 | INT 13 | WIS 14 | CHA 16\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common plus one other language\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nShortsword\n\nm 5, reach 5 ft. h6 (1d6 + 3) Piercing damage.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nUncanny Dodge\n\nactTrigger The performer is hit by an attack roll. actResponse The performer halves the damage (round down) it takes from that attack."},
  ["creature.performer-legend.xmm2024"]={title="Performer Legend",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 237\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S/M\n\nCR: 10\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 162 (25d8 + 50)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 20 | CON 14 | INT 15 | WIS 16 | CHA 20\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common plus two other languages\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe performer makes three Bejeweled Baton attacks.\n\nBejeweled Baton\n\nm 9, reach 5 ft. h10 (2d4 + 5) Bludgeoning damage plus 10 (3d6) Psychic damage.\n\nMajestic Song\n\nwis 17, each creature in a 20-foot-radius XPHB centered on a point within 120 feet. actSaveFail 22 (4d8 + 4) Psychic damage, and the target has the XPHB or XPHB condition (performer's choice) until the end of the performer's next turn. actSaveSuccess Half damage only.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nWarding Charm\n\nactTrigger A creature hits the performer with an attack roll. dwis 17, the triggering creature. actSaveFail The attack roll misses the performer, and the target has the XPHB condition until the end of the performer's next turn."},
  ["creature.performer-maestro.xmm2024"]={title="Performer Maestro",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 237\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S/M\n\nCR: 6\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 110 (17d8 + 34)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 18 | CON 14 | INT 13 | WIS 14 | CHA 19\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common plus one other language\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe performer makes three Rapier attacks.\n\nRapier\n\nm 7, reach 5 ft. h8 (1d8 + 4) Piercing damage plus 7 (2d6) Psychic damage.\n\nBeguiling Song\n\nwis 15, each creature in a 20-foot-radius XPHB centered on a point within 120 feet. actSaveFail 20 (3d10 + 4) Psychic damage, and the target has the XPHB condition until the end of the performer's next turn. actSaveSuccess Half damage only."},
  ["item.perfume.xphb2024"]={title="Perfume",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 227\n\nRaridade: none\n\nPerfume comes in a 4-ounce vial. For 1 hour after applying Perfume to yourself, you have XPHB on Charisma (XPHB) checks made to influence an Indifferent Humanoid within 5 feet of yourself."},
  ["item.perfume-vial.phb2014"]={title="Perfume (vial)",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 150\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["magicitem.perfume-of-bewitching.xdmg2024"]={title="Perfume of Bewitching",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 284\n\nRaridade: common\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 100 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 50 PO / 5 dias\n\nThis tiny vial contains magic perfume, enough for one use. You can take a XPHB action to apply the perfume to yourself, and its effect lasts 1 hour. For the duration, you have XPHB on all Charisma (XPHB and XPHB) checks made to influence a creature within 5 feet of yourself."},
  ["magicitem.perfume-of-bewitching.xge2024"]={title="Perfume of Bewitching",subtitle="Item Magico - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 138\n\nRaridade: common\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 100 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 50 PO / 5 dias\n\nThis tiny vial contains magic perfume, enough for one use. You can use an action to apply the perfume to yourself, and its effect lasts 1 hour. For the duration, you have advantage on all Charisma checks directed at humanoids of challenge rating 1 or lower. Those subjected to the perfume's effect are not aware that they've been influenced by magic."},
  ["magicitem.periapt-of-health.dmg2014"]={title="Periapt of Health",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 184\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nYou are immune to contracting any disease while you wear this pendant. If you are already infected with a disease, the effects of the disease are suppressed while you wear the pendant."},
  ["magicitem.periapt-of-health.xdmg2024"]={title="Periapt of Health",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 284\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nWhile wearing this pendant, you can take a XPHB action to regain 2d4 + 2 XPHB. Once used, this property can't be used again until the next dawn.\n\nIn addition, you have XPHB on saving throws to avoid or end the XPHB condition while you wear this pendant."},
  ["magicitem.periapt-of-proof-against-poison.dmg2014"]={title="Periapt of Proof against Poison",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 184\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nThis delicate silver chain has a brilliant-cut black gem pendant. While you wear it, poisons have no effect on you. You are immune to the poisoned condition and have immunity to poison damage."},
  ["magicitem.periapt-of-proof-against-poison.xdmg2024"]={title="Periapt of Proof against Poison",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 284\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nThis delicate silver chain has a brilliant-cut black gem pendant. While you wear it, you have XPHB to the XPHB condition and Poison damage."},
  ["magicitem.periapt-of-wound-closure.dmg2014"]={title="Periapt of Wound Closure",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 184\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nWhile you wear this pendant, you stabilize whenever you are dying at the start of your turn. In addition, whenever you roll a Hit Die to regain hit points, double the number of hit points it restores."},
  ["magicitem.periapt-of-wound-closure.xdmg2024"]={title="Periapt of Wound Closure",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 284\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nWhile wearing this pendant, you gain the following benefits.\n\nLife Preservation\n\nWhenever you make a XPHB, you can change a roll of 9 or lower to a 10, turning a failed save into a successful one.\n\nNatural Healing Boost\n\nWhenever you roll a XPHB to regain XPHB, double the number of XPHB it restores."},
  ["item.peridot.dmg2014"]={title="Peridot",subtitle="Item - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 134\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA transparent rich olive green gemstone."},
  ["item.peridot.xdmg2024"]={title="Peridot",subtitle="Item - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 214\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA rich olive green gemstone."},
  ["creature.perigee.crcotn2014"]={title="Perigee",subtitle="Criatura - CRCotN - 2014",body="Pagina: 168\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["feature.persistent-rage.phb2014.barbarian.base.15"]={title="Persistent Rage",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 46\n\nBeginning at 15th level, your rage is so fierce that it ends early only if you fall unconscious or if you choose to end it."},
  ["feature.persistent-rage.xphb2024.barbarian.base.15"]={title="Persistent Rage",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["creature.peryton.mm2014"]={title="Peryton",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 251\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 33 (6d8 + 6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20, fly: 60\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 12 | CON 13 | INT 9 | WIS 12 | CHA 10\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: understands Common and Elvish but can't speak\n\nResistencias: \n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDive Attack\n\nIf the peryton is flying and dives at least 30 feet straight toward a target and then hits it with a melee weapon attack, the attack deals an extra 9 (2d8) damage to the target.\n\nFlyby\n\nThe peryton doesn't provoke an opportunity attack when it flies out of an enemy's reach.\n\nKeen Sight and Smell\n\nThe peryton has advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on sight or smell.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe peryton makes one gore attack and one talon attack.\n\nGore\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d8 + 3) piercing damage.\n\nTalons\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h8 (2d4 + 3) piercing damage."},
  ["creature.peryton.xmm2024"]={title="Peryton",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 238\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 33 (6d8 + 6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20, fly: 60\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 12 | CON 13 | INT 9 | WIS 12 | CHA 10\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: understands Common and Elvish but can't speak\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFlyby\n\nThe peryton doesn't provoke an XPHB when it flies out of an enemy's reach.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe peryton makes one Gore attack and one Talons attack.\n\nGore\n\nm 5, reach 5 ft. h7 (1d8 + 3) Piercing damage. If the peryton moved 30+ feet straight toward the target immediately before the hit, the target takes an extra 9 (2d8) Piercing damage.\n\nTalons\n\nm 5, reach 5 ft. h8 (2d4 + 3) Piercing damage. If the attack reduces a Humanoid target to 0 XPHB, the peryton kills the target by removing its heart."},
  ["creature.pest-mascot.scc2014"]={title="Pest Mascot",subtitle="Criatura - SCC - 2014",body="Pagina: 203\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / T\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 22 (4d4 + 12)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 14 | CON 17 | INT 5 | WIS 13 | CHA 4\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nRegeneration\n\nThe pest regains 5 hit points at the start of its turn if it has at least 1 hit point. If it takes fire damage, this trait doesn't function at the start of the pest's next turn.\n\nSpiny Hide\n\nAt the start of each of its turns, the pest deals 2 (1d4) piercing damage to any creature grappling it or that it is grappling.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h4 (1d4 + 2) piercing damage."},
  ["creature.pestilence-demon.psz2014"]={title="Pestilence Demon",subtitle="Criatura - PSZ - 2014",body="Pagina: 27\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["condition.petrified.phb2014"]={title="Petrified",subtitle="Condicao - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 291\n\n• A petrified creature is transformed, along with any nonmagical object it is wearing or carrying, into a solid inanimate substance (usually stone). Its weight increases by a factor of ten, and it ceases aging.\n\n• The creature is incapacitated, can't move or speak, and is unaware of its surroundings.\n\n• Attack rolls against the creature have advantage.\n\n• The creature automatically fails Strength and Dexterity saving throws.\n\n• The creature has resistance to all damage.\n\n• The creature is immune to poison and disease, although a poison or disease already in its system is suspended, not neutralized."},
  ["condition.petrified.xphb2024"]={title="Petrified",subtitle="Condicao - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 372\n\nWhile you have the Petrified condition, you experience the following effects.\n\nTurned to Inanimate Substance\n\nYou are transformed, along with any nonmagical objects you are wearing and carrying, into a solid inanimate substance (usually stone). Your weight increases by a factor of ten, and you cease aging.\n\nIncapacitated\n\nYou have the XPHB condition.\n\nSpeed 0\n\nYour XPHB is 0 and can't increase.\n\nAttacks Affected\n\nXPHB rolls against you have XPHB.\n\nSaving Throws Affected\n\nYou automatically fail Strength and Dexterity XPHB.\n\nResist Damage\n\nYou have XPHB to all damage.\n\nPoison Immunity\n\nYou have XPHB to the XPHB condition."},
  ["magicitem.petrified-grung-egg.toa2014"]={title="Petrified Grung Egg",subtitle="Item Magico - ToA - 2014",body="Pagina: 144\n\nRaridade: unknown (magic)\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nWhile this egg is on your person, you can use an action to speak its command word and regain one expended spell slot. If the expended slot was of 4th level or higher, the new slot is 3rd level. Once you have used the egg, it can't be used again until the next dawn.\n\nAdditionally, while you are attuned to the egg, you gain resistance to poison damage.\n\nThe egg turns to dust and is destroyed if it leaves the Tomb of the Nine Gods."},
  ["creature.petrifying-death-s-head.rhw2014"]={title="Petrifying Death's Head",subtitle="Criatura - RHW - 2014",body="Pagina: 243\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / T\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 21 (6d4 + 6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 5, fly: 30\n\nSTR 8 | DEX 12 | CON 13 | INT 5 | WIS 14 | CHA 3\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nResistencias: necrotic\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: exhaustion, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFlyby\n\nThe death's head doesn't provoke an XPHB when it flies out of an enemy's reach.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nPetrifying Bite\n\nm 3, reach 5 ft. h3 (1d4 + 1) Piercing damage plus 3 (1d6) Necrotic damage. If the target is a creature, it is subjected to the following effect. con 11. 1 The target has the XPHB condition and repeats the save at the end of its next turn if it is still XPHB, ending the effect on itself on a success. 2 The target has the XPHB condition instead of the XPHB condition for 10 minutes, after which the effect ends on the target."},
  ["item.pewter-mug-with-green-spinels-brazen-coalition.psx2014"]={title="Pewter mug with green spinels (Brazen Coalition)",subtitle="Item - PSX - 2014",body="Pagina: 24\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["creature.phaerimm.mabjov2014"]={title="Phaerimm",subtitle="Criatura - MaBJoV - 2014",body="Pagina: 145\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: aberration / L\n\nCR: 15\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 170 (20d10 + 60)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 15, fly: 30\n\nSTR 20 | DEX 13 | CON 16 | INT 19 | WIS 20 | CHA 23\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Undercommon, understands Common, telepathy 100 ft.\n\nResistencias: \n\nImunidades a condicoes: petrified\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nArcane Sight\n\nThe phaerimm discerns the location of all magical auras within sight and knows which creatures within 60 feet are spellcasters.\n\nExtended Concentration\n\nThe phaerimm can concentrate on two different spells at the same time. If concentration is broken, then both spells fade immediately.\n\nImmutable Form\n\nThe phaerimm is immune to any spell or effect that would alter its form.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe phaerimm has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe phaerimm makes four Claw attacks and then makes a Bite or Stinger attack. Alternatively, it uses Spellcasting and then makes two Claw attacks.\n\nBite\n\nmw 10 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h18 (2d12 + 5) piercing damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 10 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h12 (2d6 + 5) slashing damage.\n\nStinger\n\nmw 10 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h12 (2d6 + 5) piercing damage. If the target fails a 18 Constitution saving throw, they have the paralyzed condition for 1 minute. The phaerimm's poison forces the paralyzed target to float 5 feet above the ground. The target may repeat the saving throw at the end of each of it's turns.\n\nImplant\n\nThe phaerimm makes a Stinger attack against a paralyzed target. If the stinger hits, an egg is implanted in the target. This egg can only be removed by spells that cure disease, such as lesser restoration. If the egg is not removed within 90 days, the larva emerges, and the host is killed. A phaerimm has a single egg so may only use this ability once."},
  ["creature.phaerimm-agent.fraif2014"]={title="Phaerimm Agent",subtitle="Criatura - FRAiF - 2014",body="Pagina: 269\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: aberration / L\n\nCR: 8\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 123 (19d10 + 19)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 10, fly: 40\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 18 | CON 12 | INT 17 | WIS 16 | CHA 18\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: telepathy 120 ft. understands Common and Deep Speech but can't speak\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe phaerimm has XPHB on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\nProtective Magic (3/Day)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe phaerimm makes three attacks, using Dread Stinger or Mindwarp Ray in any combination.\n\nDread Stinger\n\nm 7, reach 5 ft. h7 (1d6 + 4) Piercing damage plus 13 (2d12) Poison damage.\n\nMindwarp Ray\n\nr 7, range 120 ft. h13 (2d8 + 4) Psychic damage, and the target has the XPHB condition until the start of the phaerimm's next turn.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nTeleport\n\nThe phaerimm teleports up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space it can see."},
  ["creature.phaerimm-elder.nf2014"]={title="Phaerimm Elder",subtitle="Criatura - NF - 2014",body="=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: aberration / H\n\nCR: 14\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 218 (23d12 + 69)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 60\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 16 | CON 17 | INT 17 | WIS 16 | CHA 18\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: telepathy 120 ft. understands Common and Deep Speech but can't speak\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe phaerimm has XPHB on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\nProtective Magic (3/Day)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe phaerimm makes three Mind Lash attacks. It can replace one attack with either (A) a Vicious Stinger attack or (B) a use of Spellcasting to cast XPHB (level 3 version).\n\nMind Lash\n\nm,r 9, reach 10 ft. or range 120 ft. h32 (6d8 + 4) Psychic damage.\n\nVicious Stinger\n\nm 9, reach 5 ft. h11 (2d6 + 4) Piercing damage plus 26 (4d12) Poison damage, and the target's XPHB is reduced to 0 feet until the start of the phaerimm's next turn.\n\nSiphon Magic {@recharge 5}\n\nThe phaerimm focuses on a magic item it can see within 10 feet. When it does, the phaerimm drains the magic item of any charges. Regardless of whether charges are drained, the phaerimm can cast XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, and XPHB one additional time that day.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nTeleport\n\nThe phaerimm teleports up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space it can see."},
  ["creature.phaerimm-hatchling.fraif2014"]={title="Phaerimm Hatchling",subtitle="Criatura - FRAiF - 2014",body="Pagina: 268\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: aberration / S\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 13 (3d6 + 3)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 10, fly: 30\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 12 | CON 12 | INT 14 | WIS 16 | CHA 14\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Truesight 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: telepathy 30 ft. understands Common and Deep Speech but can't speak\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe phaerimm has XPHB on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe phaerimm makes two Stinger attacks.\n\nStinger\n\nm 3, reach 5 ft. h3 (1d4 + 1) Piercing damage."},
  ["creature.phaerimm-scout.nf2014"]={title="Phaerimm Scout",subtitle="Criatura - NF - 2014",body="=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: aberration / M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 44 (8d8 + 8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 10, fly: 40\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 13 | CON 12 | INT 15 | WIS 16 | CHA 16\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Truesight 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: telepathy 120 ft. understands Common and Deep Speech but can't speak\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe phaerimm has XPHB on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe phaerimm makes two attacks, using Stinger or Mindwarp Ray in any combination.\n\nStinger\n\nm 3, reach 5 ft. h4 (1d6 + 1) Piercing damage plus 9 (2d8) Poison damage.\n\nMindwarp Ray\n\nr 5, range 120 ft. h6 (1d6 + 3) Psychic damage, and the target has the XPHB condition until the start of the phaerimm's next turn.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nUncanny Dodge\n\nactTrigger The phaerimm is hit by an attack roll. actResponse The phaerimm halves the damage (round down) it takes from that attack."},
  ["creature.phaia.tftyp2014"]={title="Phaia",subtitle="Criatura - TftYP - 2014",body="Pagina: 132\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid"},
  ["feature.phantasmal-creatures.xphb2024.wizard.illusionist.6"]={title="Phantasmal Creatures",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["spell.phantasmal-force.phb2014"]={title="Phantasmal Force",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 2 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 264\n\nYou craft an illusion that takes root in the mind of a creature that you can see within range. The target must make an Intelligence saving throw. On a failed save, you create a phantasmal object, creature, or other visible phenomenon of your choice that is no larger than a 10-foot cube and that is perceivable only to the target for the duration. This spell has no effect on undead or constructs.\n\nThe phantasm includes sound, temperature, and other stimuli, also evident only to the creature.\n\nThe target can use its action to examine the phantasm with an Intelligence (Investigation) check against your spell save DC. If the check succeeds, the target realizes that the phantasm is an illusion, and the spell ends.\n\nWhile a target is affected by the spell, the target treats the phantasm as if it were real. The target rationalizes any illogical outcomes from interacting with the phantasm. For example, a target attempting to walk across a phantasmal bridge that spans a chasm falls once it steps onto the bridge. If the target survives the fall, it still believes that the bridge exists and comes up with some other explanation for its fall—it was pushed, it slipped, or a strong wind might have knocked it off.\n\nAn affected target is so convinced of the phantasm's reality that it can even take damage from the illusion. A phantasm created to appear as a creature can attack the target. Similarly, a phantasm created to appear as fire, a pool of acid, or lava can burn the target. Each round on your turn, the phantasm can deal 1d6 psychic damage to the target if it is in the phantasm's area or within 5 feet of the phantasm, provided that the illusion is of a creature or hazard that could logically deal damage, such as by attacking. The target perceives the damage as a type appropriate to the illusion."},
  ["spell.phantasmal-force.xphb2024"]={title="Phantasmal Force",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 2 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 304\n\nYou attempt to craft an illusion in the mind of a creature you can see within range. The target makes an Intelligence saving throw. On a failed save, you create a phantasmal object, creature, or other phenomenon that is no larger than a 10-foot XPHB and that is perceivable only to the target for the duration. The phantasm includes sound, temperature, and other stimuli.\n\nThe target can take a XPHB action to examine the phantasm with an Intelligence (XPHB) check against your spell save DC. If the check succeeds, the target realizes that the phantasm is an illusion, and the spell ends.\n\nWhile affected by the spell, the target treats the phantasm as if it were real and rationalizes any illogical outcomes from interacting with it. For example, if the target steps through a phantasmal bridge and survives the fall, it believes the bridge exists and something else caused it to fall.\n\nAn affected target can even take damage from the illusion if the phantasm represents a dangerous creature or hazard. On each of your turns, such a phantasm can deal 2d8 Psychic damage to the target if it is in the phantasm's area or within 5 feet of the phantasm. The target perceives the damage as a type appropriate to the illusion."},
  ["spell.phantasmal-killer.phb2014"]={title="Phantasmal Killer",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 4 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 265\n\nYou tap into the nightmares of a creature you can see within range and create an illusory manifestation of its deepest fears, visible only to that creature. The target must make a Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, the target becomes frightened for the duration. At the end of each of the target's turns before the spell ends, the target must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or take 4d10 psychic damage. On a successful save, the spell ends."},
  ["spell.phantasmal-killer.xphb2024"]={title="Phantasmal Killer",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 4 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 304\n\nYou tap into the nightmares of a creature you can see within range and create an illusion of its deepest fears, visible only to that creature. The target makes a Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, the target takes 4d10 Psychic damage and has XPHB on ability checks and attack rolls for the duration. On a successful save, the target takes half as much damage, and the spell ends.\n\nFor the duration, the target makes a Wisdom saving throw at the end of each of its turns. On a failed save, it takes the Psychic damage again. On a successful save, the spell ends."},
  ["item.phantasmic-circus-trinket.au2014"]={title="Phantasmic Circus Trinket",subtitle="Item - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 106\n\nRaridade: none\n\n1d6 | Trinket\n\n1 | An advertisement for a past circus performance, featuring your likeness\n\n2 | A small tin of white greasepaint\n\n3 | A green wire stem that produces an illusory flower for 1 minute when brandished dramatically\n\n4 | A fine silk ribbon, two inches wide and nine feet long\n\n5 | Bronze finger cymbals\n\n6 | A battered top hat"},
  ["background.phantasmic-circus-trouper.au2014"]={title="Phantasmic Circus Trouper",subtitle="Background - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 24\n\n• Ability Scores:\n\n• Feat:\n\n• Skill Proficiencies:\n\n• Tool Proficiencies:\n\n• Equipment:"},
  ["subclass.phantom.rhw2014.rogue.phantom.0"]={title="Phantom",subtitle="Subclasse - RHW - 2014",body="Pagina: 21\n\n=== CARACTERISTICAS DA SUBCLASSE ===\n\nNivel 3 - Phantom\n\nPagina: 62\n\nMany rogues walk a fine line between life and death, risking their own lives and taking the lives of others. While adventuring on that line, some rogues discover a mystical connection to death itself. These rogues take knowledge from the dead and become immersed in negative energy, eventually becoming like ghosts. Thieves' guilds value them as highly effective information gatherers and spies.\n\nMany shadar-kai of the Shadowfell are masters of these macabre techniques, and some are willing to teach this path. In places like Thay in the Forgotten Realms and Karrnath in Eberron, where many necromancers practice their craft, a Phantom can become a wizard's confidant and right hand. In temples of gods of death, the Phantom might work as an agent to track down those who try to cheat death and to recover knowledge that might otherwise be lost to the grave.\n\nHow did you discover this grim power? Did you sleep in a graveyard and awaken to your new abilities? Or did you cultivate them in a temple or thieves' guild dedicated to a deity of death?\n\nNivel 3 - Phantom\n\nPagina: 21\n\nEmbrace Death and Wield Ghostly Power\n\nSome Rogues traverse the veil between life and death, shepherding opponents to the grave and slipping through the world as undetectable as a spirit. In these pursuits, a Rogue might discover a mystical connection to death itself. Such an individual becomes immersed in negative energy, infusing their strikes with deathly energy and stealing knowledge from souls who have passed on. Thieves' guilds value Rogues of this persuasion as highly effective information gatherers and spies.\n\nNivel 3 - Wails from the Grave\n\nPagina: 62\n\n3rd-level Phantom feature\n\nAs you nudge someone closer to the grave, you can channel the power of death to harm someone else as well. Immediately after you deal your Sneak Attack damage to a creature on your turn, you can target a second creature that you can see within 30 feet of the first creature. Roll half the number of Sneak Attack dice for your level (round up), and the second creature takes necrotic damage equal to the roll's total, as wails of the dead sound around them for a moment.\n\nYou can use this feature a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest.\n\nNivel 3 - Wails from the Grave\n\nPagina: 21\n\nImmediately after you deal Sneak Attack damage to a creature on your turn, you can target a second creature that you can see within 30 feet of the first creature. Roll half the number of Sneak Attack damage dice for your level (round up), and the second creature takes Necrotic damage equal to the roll's total as wails of the dead sound around it.\n\nYou can use this feature a number of times equal to your Dexterity modifier (minimum of once), and you regain all expended uses when you finish a XPHB.\n\nNivel 3 - Wails from the Grave\n\nNivel 3 - Wails from the Grave\n\nNivel 3 - Whispers of the Dead\n\nPagina: 62\n\n3rd-level Phantom feature\n\nEchoes of those who have died cling to you. Whenever you finish a short or long rest, you can choose one skill or tool proficiency that you lack and gain it, as a ghostly presence shares its knowledge with you. You lose this proficiency when you use this feature to choose a different proficiency that you lack.\n\nNivel 3 - Whispers of the Dead\n\nPagina: 21\n\nWhenever you finish a XPHB or XPHB, you can choose one skill or tool proficiency that you lack and gain it, as a ghostly presence shares its knowledge with you. You lose this proficiency when you use this benefit again to choose a different proficiency.\n\nNivel 9 - Tokens of the Departed\n\nPagina: 62\n\n9th-level Phantom feature\n\nWhen a life ends in your presence, you're able to snatch a token from the departing soul, a sliver of its life essence that takes physical form: as a reaction when a creature you can see dies within 30 feet of you, you can open your free hand and cause a Tiny trinket to appear there, a soul trinket. The DM determines the trinket's form or has you roll on the phb table in the Player's Handbook to generate it. You can have a maximum number of soul trinkets equal to your proficiency bonus, and you can't create one while at your maximum.\n\nYou can use soul trinkets in the following ways:\n\n• While a soul trinket is on your person, you have advantage on death saving throws and Constitution saving throws, for your vitality is enhanced by the life essence within the object.\n\n• When you deal Sneak Attack damage on your turn, you can destroy one of your soul trinkets that's on your person and then immediately use Wails from the Grave, without expending a use of that feature.\n\n• As an action, you can destroy one of your soul trinkets, no matter where it's located. When you do so, you can ask the spirit associated with the trinket one question. The spirit appears to you and answers in a language it knew in life. It's under no obligation to be truthful, and it answers as concisely as possible, eager to be free. The spirit knows only what it knew in life, as determined by the DM.\n\nNivel 9 - Tokens of the Departed\n\nPagina: 22\n\nThe spirits of the dead are drawn to you, and echoes of their past lives magically manifest as strange curios with resonant power.\n\nYou gain two soul trinkets. A soul trinket is a Tiny object (the DM determines the trinket's form or has you roll on the XPHB in the XPHB to generate it). If you move more than 30 feet from a trinket, the trinket immediately teleports to you, appearing somewhere on your person.\n\nUsing Soul Trinkets\n\nYou can use soul trinkets in the following ways:\n\n• Death's Knell\n\n• Life Essence\n\n• Spirit Query\n\nGaining Additional Soul Trinkets\n\nWhen a creature you can see within 30 feet of you dies, you can take a XPHB to gain another soul trinket, claiming a sliver of that creature's departing spirit. The new trinket appears somewhere on your person.\n\nYou can have a maximum of two soul trinkets at a time. If you try to gain a soul trinket while at your maximum, one of your existing trinkets is immediately destroyed and replaced by the new trinket. The maximum number of soul trinkets you can have increases when you reach Rogue levels 13 (three trinkets) and 17 (four trinkets).\n\nWhenever you finish a XPHB with fewer than two soul trinkets, you gain soul trinkets until you have two.\n\nNivel 9 - Tokens of the Departed\n\nNivel 9 - Voice of Death\n\nPagina: 22\n\nYou can cast XPHB once without a spell slot, requiring no spell components and using Dexterity as the spellcasting modifier. You regain the ability to cast it this way when you finish a Short or Long Rest.\n\nWhen you cast the spell, you can target one of your soul trinkets from Tokens of the Departed instead of a corpse, allowing the spirit of the creature associated with the trinket to answer.\n\nNivel 9 - Voice of Death\n\nNivel 13 - Ghost Walk\n\nPagina: 62\n\n13th-level Phantom feature\n\nYou can phase partially into the realm of the dead, becoming like a ghost. As a bonus action, you assume a spectral form. While in this form, you have a flying speed of 10 feet, you can hover, and attack rolls have disadvantage against you. You can also move through creatures and objects as if they were difficult terrain, but you take 1d10 force damage if you end your turn inside a creature or an object.\n\nYou stay in this form for 10 minutes or until you end it as a bonus action. To use this feature again, you must finish a long rest or destroy one of your soul trinkets as part of the bonus action you use to activate Ghost Walk.\n\nNivel 13 - Ghost Walk\n\nPagina: 23\n\nAs a XPHB, you assume a spectral form, gaining the benefits below for 10 minutes or until you end them (no action required). Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a XPHB unless you destroy one of your soul trinkets from Tokens of the Departed (no action required) to restore your use of it.\n\nFlight\n\nYou gain a XPHB of 10 feet and can hover.\n\nHazy Form\n\nAttack rolls have XPHB against you.\n\nIncorporeal Movement\n\nYou can move through creatures and objects as if they were XPHB, but you take 1d10 Force damage if you end your turn inside a creature or an object.\n\nNivel 13 - Ghost Walk\n\nNivel 17 - Death's Friend\n\nPagina: 62\n\n17th-level Phantom feature\n\nYour association with death has become so close that you gain the following benefits:\n\n• When you use your Wails from the Grave, you can deal the necrotic damage to both the first and the second creature.\n\n• At the end of a long rest, a soul trinket appears in your hand if you don't have any soul trinkets, as the spirits of the dead are drawn to you.\n\nNivel 17 - Death's Friend\n\nPagina: 23\n\nYour association with death has become so close that you gain the following benefits.\n\nDeath's Lament\n\nWhen you use Wails from the Grave, you can deal the feature's Necrotic damage to both the first and the second creature.\n\nDraw of Death\n\nWhen you roll XPHB, you gain one soul trinket for your Tokens of the Departed if you have none remaining."},
  ["feature.phantom.rhw2014.rogue.phantom.3"]={title="Phantom",subtitle="Caracteristica - RHW - 2014",body="Pagina: 21\n\nEmbrace Death and Wield Ghostly Power\n\nSome Rogues traverse the veil between life and death, shepherding opponents to the grave and slipping through the world as undetectable as a spirit. In these pursuits, a Rogue might discover a mystical connection to death itself. Such an individual becomes immersed in negative energy, infusing their strikes with deathly energy and stealing knowledge from souls who have passed on. Thieves' guilds value Rogues of this persuasion as highly effective information gatherers and spies."},
